Brazil,BRA,19. Must a State employing the right of self-defense in response to a cyber operation or operations constituting an armed attack report its actions to the UN Security Council?,Yes,"“Moreover, self-defense should be a temporary remedy. Member states that exercise their right to self-defense must immediately report it to the Security Council, in line with article 51 of the Charter.”","UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contribution, pg. 20, ¶ 4, (2021)",https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Brazil/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions(2021).pdf?CID=b36d6b07-0f1d-4d0a-a113-a36611671044,
Canada,CAN,1. Does Article 51 of the UN Charter apply in the cyber context?,Yes,“Canada considers that the inherent right of self-defence if an armed attack occurs against a State also applies in cyberspace.”,"Canada Statement on International Law Applicable in Cyberspace, pg. 19, ¶ 46 (2022)",https://perma.cc/HNH3-BX5J,
