Canada,CAN,12. Can a cyber operation alone constitute an armed attack for purposes of triggering the right of self-defense?,Yes,Canada considers that the inherent right of self-defence if an armed attack  occurs against a State also applies in cyberspace   “Cyber activities may amount to such a threat or use of force where the scale and effects are comparable to those from other operations that constitute the use of force at international law.”,"Canada Statement on International Law Applicable in Cyberspace, pg. 19, ¶ 45 (2022)",https://perma.cc/HNH3-BX5J,
