Canada,CAN,17. Can non-affected States exercise collective self-defense in response to a cyber operation or operations constituting an armed attack against an affected State?,Yes,“The right to self-defence is both an individual and collective right of States.”,"Canada Statement on International Law Applicable in Cyberspace, pg. 19, ¶ 45 (2022)",https://perma.cc/HNH3-BX5J,
Canada,CAN,17(a) Must a State exercising collective self-defense in response to a cyber operation(s) constituting an armed attack have the victim state request or consent to such actions?,Silent,,,,
