Chile,CHL,1. Does Article 51 of the UN Charter apply in the cyber context?,Yes,"“The Republic of Chile has stated, through its National Cyber-Defense Policy, that it will refrain from resorting to the threat of the use or the use of force through cyberspace in a manner that is against international law, and that it will exercise its right to self-defense against any armed attack carried out through cyberspace, in accordance with the provisions of Article 51 of the United Nations Charter.”","OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response Submitted by Chile, pg. 1, Question 2",https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:w:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Chile/Response%20by%20Chile.%20EN%20(1).DOCX?d=w88cf4e2dd83649f199b19e1fe85fe80c&csf=1&web=1&e=zsyWB2,
