Ecuador,ECU,11)Must a cyber operation involve the use of a weapon or weapons to qualify as an armed attack?,Silent,,OAS Survey Response Submitted by Ecuador,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/iLITHome/IQCnwd0Jqcv_QqwRRxQs5NbrAcGo4Q-lORKcLhHJ8y3ol3w?email=michellexin%40temple.edu&e=M43Dw5,
Ecuador,ECU,12)Can a cyber operation alone constitute an armed attack for purposes of triggering the right of self-defense?,Yes,"“According to NATO, a cyber attack is 'an offensive or defensive cyber operation that is intended to cause injury or kill people or to damage or destroy objects.' According to this concept, it can be considered an armed attack.”",OAS Survey Response Submitted by Ecuador,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/iLITHome/IQCnwd0Jqcv_QqwRRxQs5NbrAcGo4Q-lORKcLhHJ8y3ol3w?email=michellexin%40temple.edu&e=M43Dw5,
Ecuador,ECU,12a)Must a decision that a cyber operation constitute an armed attack triggering a right of self-defense be made on a case-by-case basis or by considering all the circumstances?,Silent,,OAS Survey Response Submitted by Ecuador,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/iLITHome/IQCnwd0Jqcv_QqwRRxQs5NbrAcGo4Q-lORKcLhHJ8y3ol3w?email=michellexin%40temple.edu&e=M43Dw5,
Ecuador,ECU,12b) Can a cyber operation qualify as an armed attack under article 51 of the UN Charter if the effects generated are comparable to effects resulting from an action that would otherwise qualify as an armed attack?,Silent,"According to NATO, a cyber attack is ""an offensive or defensive cyber operation that is intended to cause injury or kill people or to damage or destroy objects."" According to this concept, it can be considered an armed attack.”",OAS Survey Response Submitted by Ecuador,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/s/iLITHome/IQCnwd0Jqcv_QqwRRxQs5NbrAcGo4Q-lORKcLhHJ8y3ol3w?email=michellexin%40temple.edu&e=M43Dw5,
