Estonia,EST,1)Does Article 51 of the UN Charter apply in the cyber context?,Yes,"“In accordance with Article 51 of the UN Charter, states have the right for self-defence in the case of an armed attack” Estonia believes that cyber operations that cause injury or death to persons, damage or destruction could amount to an armed attack under the UN Charter",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary Nat’l Contributions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Estonia/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions%20(2021).pdf,
