Estonia,EST,2a)Is the scope of any independent right of self-defense co-extensive with the obligations assumed under Article 51 of the UN Charter,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,3)Does a State’s right of self-defense apply to actions conducted by non-state actors acting without the involvement of another State(s)?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4)Is the right of self-defense triggered solely if an armed attack is attributable to a State according to the applicable rules of customary international law of State responsibility?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4a)Can a State  exercise self-defense on the basis that the territorial state would be “unwilling and unable” to repress non-state actors whose cyber operations have extraterritorial effects that would rise to the level of an armed attack if conducted by a State?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,5)Is the exercise of the right of self-defense subject to the principle of necessity?,Yes,"“In such a situation, the injured state has the right to self-defence considering all applicable restrictions of the UN Charter and customary international law, such as proportionality and necessity.”",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary Nat’l Contributions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Estonia/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions%20(2021).pdf,
Estonia,EST,5a)Must force be the only option available to successfully repel and armed attack under the right of self-defense?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,6)Is the exercise of the right of self-defense subject to the principle of proportionality?,Yes,"“In such a situation, the injured state has the right to self-defence considering all applicable restrictions of the UN Charter and customary international law, such as proportionality and necessity.”",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary Nat’l Contributions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Estonia/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions%20(2021).pdf,
