Estonia,EST,12e) Can any unlawful cyber use of force in violation of Art. 2(4) of the UN Charter trigger a State’s right of self-defense?,Ambiguous,"“Estonia believes that cyber operations that cause injury or death to persons, damage or destruction could amount to an armed attack under the UN Charter.”",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary Nat'l Contributions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Estonia/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions%20(2021).pdf,
