Estonia,EST,"18)In its response to a cyber operation or operations qualifying as an armed attack, is the injured state limited to cyber means in response?",No,"“In its response to an armed attack by cyber means, the injured state is not necessarily limited to taking measures by cyber means – all means remain reserved to states in order to respond to an armed attack in a manner that is proportionate and in accordance with other provisions of international law.”",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary Nat’l Contributions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Estonia/UNGA%20Official%20Compendium%20of%20Voluntary%20National%20Contributions%20(2021).pdf,
