Finland,FIN,12g)Can losses of functionality from a cyber operation without accompanying death or injury or damage or destruction to property constitute an armed attack?,Silent,,,,
Finland,FIN,"12h)Can cyber operations producing significant economic effects such as the collapse of a State’s financial system, or the degradation of parts of its economy or critical infrastructure qualify as an armed attack?",No,"A question has also been raised, whether a cyberattack  producing significant economic effects such as the collapse of a State’s financial system or parts of its economy should be equated to an armed attack. This question merits further consideration.",International Law and Cyberspace: Finland’s National Positions,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Finland/Finland%20Statements.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=IeB5Tf,
Finland,FIN,13)Can cyber operations that individually fall below the threshold of an armed attack aggregate into an armed attack triggering the right of self-defense?,Silent,,,,
