Ireland,IRL,1)Does Article 51 of the UN Charter apply in the cyber context?,Yes,28. A cyber-operation that by virtue of its scale and effects reaches the threshold of an armed attack would permit the exercise of self-defence in accordance with Article 51 and customary international law.,Ireland Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Ireland/Ireland%20(2023)%20National-Position-Paper.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=NgmrTg,
