New Zealand,NZL,12)Can a cyber operation alone constitute an armed attack for purposes of triggering the right of self-defense?,Yes,26. A state subjected to malicious cyber activity amounting to an armed attack has further recourse to the inherent right of individual and/or collective self-defence in accordance with Article 51 of the UN Charter,"New Zealand, The Application of International Law to State Activity in Cyberspace",https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/New%20Zealand/New%20Zealand%20(2025).pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=iE0MfM,
