New Zealand,NZL,12b) Can a cyber operation qualify as an armed attack under article 51 of the UN Charter if the effects generated are comparable to effects resulting from an action that would otherwise qualify as an armed attack?,Yes,Cyber activity that amounts to a use of force will also constitute an armed attack for the  purposes of Article 51 of the UN Charter if it results in effects of a scale and nature equivalent to those caused by a kinetic armed attack.,"New Zealand, The Application of International Law to State Activity in Cyberspace",https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/New%20Zealand/New%20Zealand%20(2025).pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=iE0MfM,
