Sweden,SWE,1)Does Article 51 of the UN Charter apply in the cyber context?,Yes,"Under Article 51 of the UN Charter, States have a right of self-defence if an armed attack occurs. An attack by cyber means may have the  potential to constitute an armed attack if its scale and effects are comparable  to an armed attack by kinetic means.",Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=2GIU3a,
