Sweden,SWE,3)Does a State’s right of self-defense apply to actions conducted by non-state actors acting without the involvement of another State(s)?,Silent,,,,
Sweden,SWE,4)Is the right of self-defense triggered solely if an armed attack is attributable to a State according to the applicable rules of customary international law of State responsibility?,Silent,,,,
Sweden,SWE,4a)Can a State  exercise self-defense on the basis that the territorial state would be “unwilling and unable” to repress non-state actors whose cyber operations have extraterritorial effects that would rise to the level of an armed attack if conducted by a State?,Silent,,,,
Sweden,SWE,5)Is the exercise of the right of self-defense subject to the principle of necessity?,Yes,"Any use of force in the exercise of self-defence, including through cyber means, needs to adhere to principles of necessity and proportionality.",Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=2GIU3a,
