United Kingdom,GBR,17)Can non-affected States exercise collective self-defense in response to a cyber operation or operations constituting an armed attack against an affected State?,Yes,"An operation carried out by cyber means may constitute an armed attack giving rise to the inherent right of individual or collective self-defence, as recognised in Article 51 of the UN Charter....",Application of international law to state’s conduct in cyberspace: UK Statement,https://tuprd.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iLITHome/iLIT%20Student%20Researchers/Global%20Cyber%20Law/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/United%20Kingdom/United%20Kingdom_2021%20Policy%20Paper_Application%20of%20international%20law%20to%20states’%20conduct%20in%20cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=E5ah65,
